ects USD/JPY to fall longer-term; last 83.54 vs 83.88 hit earlier. EUR/JPY falling due to profit-taking orders by speculators; last 114.94 vs 115.07 earlier, support at 114.50. EUR/USD last at 1.3759, may trade in 1.3720-1.3780 band. (takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0335 GMT [Dow Jones] Volatilities implied by 1-month ATM USD/JPY options higher in Tokyo at 10.85%/11.55% vs 10.50%/11.20% Friday in New York, as players seek hedges against downside in spot amid lingering speculation Fed may ease more aggressively than BOJ, which concludes two-day policy-setting meeting Tuesday. Rise in vols comes after \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York\uc2  President Dudley said Friday Fed is almost certain to take further easing measures ahead as current economic conditions are "wholly unsatisfactory." Vols may trend up further this week if Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not meet or exceed market expectations for it to expand liquidity-provision measures, dealers say.(andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0333 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares down 1.6% at 444.45, with investors selling after brokerage firms said companies received permission to issue new equity valued at VND34.6 trillion in 3Q vs VND18.6 trillion in 1H, causing concerns that large volumes of new shares will result in price dilution. "In addition to weak inflows, the glut of new shares will certainly pull down prices," says brokerage trader. Volume thin with 36 million shares valued at VND840 billion traded so far. Among decliners, Ocean Group (OGC.VH) down 4.1% at VND30,300, Itaco (ITA.VH) down 4.2% at VND16,300, \uc2 Sacombank\uc2  (STB.VH) down 2.4% at VND16,500. Tips immediate support at 442. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com) [ 10-04-10 0014ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101004e6a40002r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
