\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Dutch Name Buying JPY Crosses - Dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 1,436 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2010\par 03:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0146 GMT [Dow Jones] Strong buying of yen-crosses by Dutch bank in past 20 minutes propelled EUR/JPY from 114.90 to as high as 115.07, USD/JPY from 83.40 to 83.65, say Singapore-based dealers; reckon rise was not due to any official \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Add, Japanese and UK names also grabbing USD/JPY offers. USD/JPY last at 83.57, EUR/JPY at 114.96. (jerry.tan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0146 GMT [Dow Jones] October HSI futures +0.7% at 22,486, as cash market expected to open higher on Wall Street cue. Still, contract ended Thursday at recently rare 30-point discount to cash, suggesting view that profit-taking may set in for HSI in near term, which unsurprising given HSI's 9% rise in September. October open interest increases 316 lots to 108,779. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0144 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan shares +0.6% at 8289.36, hitting 8-month high 8300.04 earlier, led by HTC's (2498.TW) 1.0% rise in hops of strong September revenues, says Mega International Investment Service manager Stanley Chou. Notes profit-taking likely to cap Taiex's gains, though any correction likely mild; "The Taiex is not likely to fall sharply" as people still buying large-cap stocks, he says. Tips Taiex in 8200-8300 band for rest of session. Yulon Motor (2201.TW) +5.6% at NT$60.20. \uc2 Nan Ya Plastics\uc2  (1303.TW) down 3.5% at NT$66.10 after fire hits company's plant Sunday, which will cause estimated NT$150 million in revenue losses, according to company's spokesman. (mason.wu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0142 GMT [Dow Jones] KLCI +0.6% at 1474.75, supported by strong gains in regional markets, but dealers say upside likely limited in near term due to lack of positive domestic drivers. Tip strong resistance at 1480. Still, analysts say market's long-term uptrend remains intact, underpinned by positive chart patterns, expected roll-out of large government projects. HwangDBS Vickers Research says KLCI may reach 1525-1565 before 2010 is over. "This means there is a potential for the bellwether to match or exceed its all-time record high of 1524.69," HwangDBS says. Among gainers, \uc2 MMC Corp\uc2  (2194.KU) +5.4% at MYR3.29, Top Glove (7113.KU) +4.3% at MYR5.59, Kencana (5122.KU) +4.8% at MYR1.73. Among decliners, \uc2 JT International\uc2  (2615.KU) down 0.9% at MYR5.63. (benjamin.low@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0142 GMT [Dow Jones] Copper, aluminum, zinc and nickel all edge higher in early trade; tin and lead so far untraded, reflecting Chinese holiday-affected trading conditions. LME 3-month copper most active at $8,145/ton, up $50 since Friday's kerb with 86 lots done. \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  says in report that 4Q could intially see more gains. "Considering that market participants seem to slowly factor in higher emerging market growth next year and considering that some investors are still underweight copper, we believe that prices may rise further at the outset of 4Q10." But adds copper could correct later in quarter with inventory trend possibly reversing if seasonal pattern follows traditional trajectory. Also notes Chinese imports could fall; "weak incentives for copper imports from China are at present also reflected in differentials between the Shanghai Futures Exchange and the London Metals Exchange prices, which have been firmly against importers since August." (james.campbell@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0140 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares likely to rise, but profit taking likely amid volatile trade as key 1,000 level approached. "Nothing has changed fundamentally. Fund inflows are still the key to this upward sentiment. However, while the market seems to be confident that the index will head to the 1,000 mark, investors are aware that several stocks are in overbought zones," says KT Zmico Securities First VP Charoen Iamphattanatham. Adds energy heavyweights like PTT (PTT.TH), \uc2 PTT Exploration & Production\uc2  (PTTEP.TH) likely to dominate while gains in "overbought" banks may be slower after recent rises. Initial resistance pegged at 987, support at 963. SET Index ends +0.3% at fresh 14-year high close of 978.58 Friday. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0140 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY, EUR/JPY rise as Japanese importers buy, amid lingering caution over possible Japanese government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at major European bank. Says USD/JPY may test 84.00 vs last 83.56 (up from earlier low 83.22). But says absent any Japanese government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , "the dollar-yen should stay pretty heavily offered this week," due to broad-based USD weakness amid mounting expectations for further Fed easing; that should curb any sharp rises in pair for week, dealer says. EUR/JPY rises to 115.07 (from earlier low 114.61), highest since May 18; last 114.96. But says profit-taking by short-term investors may drag on any further rises in cross, likely keeping it centered around 115.00 for now.(andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0137 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/HKD tad higher as local bank buys, says senior trader at Chinese bank; tips pair in 7.7580-7.7610 band near term. "The pair is likely to remain in tight range as Chinese markets are closed. Still, the expected rise in local stocks could lure inflows, lending support to the pair," trader adds. Pair last at 7.7603 vs 7.7601 late Thursday; Hong Kong financial markets closed Friday for public holiday. (chester.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0130 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore stocks in broad-based advance, with almost 4 gainers for every decliner. STI +0.3% at 3139.08, with resistance expected at 3184 (peak at June 6, 2008). "It's not a strong start for the week but considering that the index is already at its highest in more than two years, the performance is credible. With third-quarter earnings up ahead, the market could head higher if results beat expectations and guidance is strong," dealer says. Chinese shipbuilders active following China's announcement of US$5 billion fund to help Greek shipping companies buy Chinese vessels. Cosco (F83.SG) +2.2% at S$1.85, JES (EG0.SG) +2.9% at S$0.36, Yangzijiang (BS6.SG) +1.1% at S$1.80. (frankie.ho@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0128 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/KRW falls to 1,124.5 vs 1,130.4 late Friday in Seoul as downward momentum remains intact after swift breach of 1,130 support at market open. But further downside limited around current levels with investors increasingly wary over possible USD buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as pair now trading at 5-month lows, while government reiterates earlier today it will act against sharp one-sided moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. "I don't think the pair will fall below 1,120. The dollar is down by about 5 won already today (vs last close)," says local bank trader. Notes offshore players selling USD again, but their selling not as aggressive as Friday. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0126 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR steady at 8,920 despite broad USD weakness vs regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as players see chances of Bank Indonesia continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  increasing after IDR's recent sharp gains, dealers say; "But, the tone is still bearish on the dollar because foreigners may still need to buy the rupiah to settle their purchases of Indonesian stocks and bonds done Friday," dealer with foreign bank says. 8,910-8,930 range tipped. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0113 GMT [Dow Jones] Stock selection "makes all the difference" in September, will again be important in October, says local fund manager; notes HSI up 9% in September, which impressive, but even more impressive are \uc2 Hutchison Whampoa\uc2  (0013.HK), HKEx (0388.HK), \uc2 SHK Properties\uc2  (0016.HK) racking up 26%, 25%, 23% rises last month, vs China Life (2628.HK), Esprit (0330.HK) at other extreme, up 3% and down 3% respectively. Thinks gains will moderate in October, strategy is to buy "strong stocks" on pullback rather than betting on laggards to catch up. Tips HSI to open modestly higher today on Wall Street cues, although profit-taking likely to set in early part of week, if not today. HSI ends Thursday down 0.1% at 22,358.17. (robert.li@dowjones.com) [ 10-03-10 2147ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101004e6a400017\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
