\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:USD/JPY May Rise To 84.0 If BOJ Moves Aggressively\b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2010\par 01:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 2349 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY may rise to 84.00 if BOJ decides at policy board meeting to buy more long-term JGBs or asset-backed securities, says Akira Hoshino, senior dealer at \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ. Adds move would send message that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  taking steps in quantitative easing. Nikkei reports today that BOJ may take bolder-than-anticipated steps, such as buying ABSs. Hoshino adds that if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, coordinating with BOJ's moves, pair may rise above 85.00. On the other hand, says that with expectations for some more modest steps already factored in pair may fall to below 83.00, approaching level that triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mid-September, if BOJ meeting only comes up with easing measures such as expanding 3-month, 6-month lending facilities introduced last December, August respectively. Pair last at 83.57 on small rising trend during early Asia morning. Says EUR/USD may fall to 1.3550 as correction comes in recent USD weakness.\par \par \uc2  EUR/USD falls Monday after hitting highest level since March at 1.3809 as extent of Ireland's budget deficit revealed; pair last 1.3679. Says EUR/JPY may trade in 113.00-115.00 range vs last 114.33. (kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 04-10-10 2349GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1012 1037 1085 5011 55117 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI00000