\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/JPY Eyeing Pre- \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  82.87 Low -Dealer\b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2010\par 01:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 2320 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY likely to be weighed by broad-based USD weakness in Asia, with players closely focused on 82.87, 15-year low marked just before \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sep. 15, says Osao Iizuka, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at \uc2 Sumitomo Trust\uc2  and Banking. Following comments Friday by \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York\uc2  President Dudley that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost certain to opt for further easing, Bank of Japan could further pressure USD/JPY down this week if it fails to impress markets with any additional easing measures of its own at end of regular 2-day policy-setting meeting Tuesday, Iizuka says. "While concern over further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may keep the dollar supported above Y82.87 for today, the BOJ meeting tomorrow could bring that level closer in sight, depending on the outcome." Pair last 83.33. Says USD weakness means more rises may be in store for EUR/USD. After pair earlier tops 1.3800, its highest since March 17, says could rise to 1.3850 later in global day. Last 1.3778.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile EUR/JPY may trade in band around 115.00, last 114.82.(andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 03-10-10 2320GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1012 1037 1085 5011 55117 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101003e6a30005f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
