\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Tin, Copper Look To Challenge 2008 Highs\b0\par\par\uc2 1,760 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2010\par 01:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 2358 GMT [Dow Jones] Base metals picture looking positive with tin approaching 2008 record high of $25,500/ton after LME 3-month contract added $700 to close at $24,900 Friday. Copper also well bid with 2006 high at $8,800 and record of $8,940 hit in 2008 likely to be challenged later in year based on inventory trend, expectations of renewed China demand. LME 3-month copper closes at 2-year high of $8,095 +$85 after good China PMI readings last week. LME Options declaration this Wedneday likely supportive. "The main open strikes suggest that aluminium is likely to hold above the $2,300 level and copper above $8,000," says Sucden Financial. LME 3-month aluminum added $8 to $2,358/ton Friday. However trade likely to be subdued in Asia this week with China closed until Friday for national day holidays. Data focus likely to be on U.S. September non-farm payrolls Friday. Later today, euro-zone August PPI due at 0900 GMT, U.S. August pending home sales index at 1400 GMT, only data of note. Culmination of Ryder cup golf competition in European session, early U.S. could hurt trading volumes. (james.campbell@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2358 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore government bonds likely to trade in range with yields moving 2-3 bps either way as investors look for further cues on outlook for global economy, says trader with foreign bank. "For today, we'll see how equities perform. If stocks turn high, we might see some selling in bonds, but the moves won't be big." On Friday, 2-year bond yield up 1 bp to close at 0.42%, while 10-year up 2 bps to end at 2.04%. (venkat.pr@dowjones.com