e attitude since they want to see policy developments from the BOJ (policy board) meeting," says Yutaka Miura, senior technical analyst at Mizuho Securities. Adds market players cautious USD/JPY (now 83.35) may still weaken even if BOJ announces additional monetary easing on Tuesday unless surprise steps come out. Puts today's Nikkei range at 9350-9500 vs 9404.23 (+0.4%) Friday close. Euro-linked shares like \uc2 Sony\uc2  (6758.TO) may rise on firmer EUR/JPY (now 114.85); commodity-related stocks expected to advance on rise in crude and gold prices Friday. Nikkei 225 December futures ended Chicago trading at 9435 vs Osaka close at 9390 Friday. (kana.inagaki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2303 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/SGD hits new low at 1.3108 in New York trade Friday, tracking USD's slide vs EUR, majors given possibility of U.S. Federal Reserve's quantitative measures to support economy. Investors chasing higher-yielding assets, as worries remain that low interest rate regime in U.S. may continue for extended period. Immediate psychological support at 1.3000. Pair now 1.3117 vs 1.3159 late Asia trade Friday. (venkat.pr@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2300 GMT [Dow Jones] PREVIEW: Hong Kong August retail sales growth likely remained in double digits, but likely slowed vs July on fading base factor. By value, tipped +16.0% on-year in August vs July's +18.9%; by volume +13.2% in August vs July's +16.0%, according to Dow Jones poll of 5 economists. "Domestic demand remains buoyant with the fall in the jobless rate and tourist arrivals continue to be resilient, but the higher base of comparison last year also weighs on the headline figure," Core Pacific-Yamaichi analyst Keith Lo says. \uc2 Bank of East Asia\uc2  economist Paul Tang says retail sales growth likely fell to "high single digits" in 4Q due to higher base of comparison, as city's retail sales returned to growth since September last year. Data due 0830 GMT. (chester.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2256 GMT [Dow Jones] A