\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  to ease  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 's money mkt impact-source\b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2010\par 12:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month for first time in 6 years\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't changed trend for yen strength\par \par \uc2 * For more on Japan's economy, click [ID:nECONJP]\par \par \uc2 (Adds economist)\par \par \uc2 By Sumio Ito\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 1 (Reuters) - Japan's government will consult with the Bank of Japan to make sure the redemption of financing bills (FBs) issued to fund its recent yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not disrupt money markets and cause interest rates to rise, a government source told Reuters on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last month for the first time in more than six years, selling 2.1249 trillion yen ($25.44 billion) in the month to Sept. 28, to stem a yen rise that is threatening Japan's fragile economic recovery. [ID:nTOE68T08I]\par \par \uc2 By law, the government does not have the right to print cash and has to fund its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by issuing financing bills (FBs). It sets the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amount and the BOJ, which has the right to print cash, acts as its agent and temporarily underwrites the bills.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ then sells yen, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  must eventually pay back the BOJ by selling the same amount of FBs in the money market.\par \par \uc2 "Signals from authorities are a big issue at the moment," said Masamichi Adachi, senior economist at \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "But there are excess reserves in Japan's financial system, so the market can absorb the FB issuance. Theoretically, this should have no impact on interest rates, but sometimes there are misunderstandings."\par \par \uc2 The source said the government would deal appropriately with the sale of the FBs in consultation with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while taking into account its coffers and the impact on markets.\par \par \uc2 The government stance shows its intention to collaborate with the BOJ in keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised, to maximise the benefits of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The BOJ has so far left the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised by allowing the yen selling to expand the money supply. The government is likely to explicitly pressure the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue leaving \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised and to ease policy in other ways to maximise the benefits of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a departure from the usual \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  practice of absorbing the extra funds through issuance of government bills, effectively make \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  a part of a monetary loosening mix. (Writing by Tetsushi Kajimoto and Stanley White; Editing by Nathan Layne and Edmund Klamann)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101001e6a100146\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
