\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Noda: to act decisively on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  when needed\b0\par\par\uc2 145 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2010\par 03:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (For more stories on the Japanese economy, click [ID:nECONJP])\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 1 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said on Friday he would continue to take decisive steps on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves when necessary.\par \par \uc2 He declined to comment when asked about the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Noda told a news conference after a cabinet meeting the economy is recovering slowly but remains in a severe situation and he was closely watching downside risks in taking policy steps.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities conducted a total of 2.1249 trillion yen ($25.37 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the latest month to Sept. 28, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday. (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Edwina Gibbs)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/NODA (URGENT)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101001e6a10002h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
