\uc2 \f2 South Korea's inflation rate shot to a 17-month high in September due to a spike in food prices, while the nation's average daily export value was the highest on record, prompting economists to forecast the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may raise its policy rate this month. (published 0511 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: INDONESIA SEPT INFLATION EASES, PUSHING BACK RATE EXPECTATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in Indonesia eased in September, pushing back expectations of the timing of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's next rate increase. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER RENEWS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THREAT \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister renewed his pledge Friday to take "decisive" steps to fight the yen's rise, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  edges back toward last month's 15-year high against the dollar that triggered Tokyo's first market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in more than six years. (published 0249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ: CONSUMER SENTIMENT WORSENS FOR FIRST TIME IN SIX QUARTERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sentiment among Japanese consumers deteriorated for the first time in six quarters in July-September, a Bank of Japan survey showed Friday, suggesting that an uncertain economic outlook is starting to weigh more heavily on the household sector. (published 0650 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: INDIA AUG EXPORTS UP 22.5% ON YEAR AT $16.64 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's merchandise exports rose 22.5% to $16.64 billion in August from a year earlier, provisional data issued Friday by the Ministry of Commerce showed. (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA SEPTEMBER \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  MANUFACTURING PMI 48.8 VS 50.9 IN AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in South Korea's manufacturing sector slowed for a fifth straight month in September, with a key gauge measuring activity falling below the neutral level for the first time in 19 months, amid escalating concerns over the strength of the global economic recovery. (published 0050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA: GOVERNMENT DEBT ESTIMATED TO RISE TO KRW400.4 TLN AT END 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's government debt load is expected to rise to KRW400.4 trillion, or 34.7% of gross domestic product, by the end of this year, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Friday. (published 0600 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA TO REMOVE TARIFFS ON CABBAGE, RADISH IMPORTS BY END-2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea will temporarily remove its tariffs on cabbage and radish imports and buy 150 tons of the fresh vegetables from China in an effort to help curb soaring fresh vegetable prices, the Ministry of Food, Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries said Friday. (published 0308 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA SEPTEMBER PERFORMANCE OF MANUFACTURING INDEX -4.4 POINTS TO 47.3 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's manufacturing sector contracted in September for the first time this year as factory production was hit hard by a strong local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and rising costs, a performance gauge produced by an industry group published Friday shows. (published 2330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: THAI SEPTEMBER CPI UP 3.0% ON YEAR VS EXPECTED 3.3% RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's consumer price index rose 3.0% in September from a year earlier, compared with a 3.3% increase in August, the Commerce Ministry's Permanent Secretary Yanyong Phuangrach said Friday. (published 0329 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : COMMERCIAL BANKS' JAN-AUG LOANS UP 7% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday loans of commercial banks grew 7% on year during the first eight months of this year, and the outlook for loan growth for the rest of the year remains positive, in line with the improving domestic economy. (published 0449 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE 3Q PRIVATE HOME PRICES UP 3.1% VS 5.3% IN 2Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's private residential-property prices rose 3.1% in the third quarter from the previous three months, slowing from the second quarter's 5.3% rise, according to flash estimates issued by the government Friday. (published 0436 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: MOST ECONOMISTS EXPECT BOJ TO EXPAND LIQUIDITY NEXT WEEK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan is expected to take more monetary easing steps at its two-day policy board meeting starting Monday, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's own business sentiment survey reveals deepening concerns about the outlook for the corporate sector and the yen's uptrend shows no signs of abating, a Dow Jones Newswires poll showed. (published 0539 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: HYUNDAI GROUP, M+W GROUP TO PARTNER FOR HYUNDAI ENGINEERING BID \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday it will bid for a controlling stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Engineering & Construction Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . in partnership with German engineering firm M+W Group. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LG ELECTRONICS\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' HANDSET, TV DIVISION CHIEFS REPLACED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LG Electronics Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's third-largest seller of cellphones, said Friday it has replaced the chief executives of its handset and television divisions. (published 0156 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SK ENERGY BOARD APPROVES PLAN TO SPIN OFF REFINING, CHEMICAL BUSINESSES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SK Energy Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., South Korea's largest oil refiner by capacity, said Friday that its board has approved a restructuring plan, under which it will spin off its refining and chemical businesses into two separate companies. (published 0149 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHAMP'S HEALTHCARE AUSTRALIA LIKELY TO SELL FOR AROUND A$150M -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More than three parties are taking a serious look at Australia-based CHAMP Private Equity's Healthcare Australia, or HCA, in what is expected to be a roughly A$150 million sale, a person familiar with the matter told Dow Jones Newswires Friday. (published 0534 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOWER SEEKS TO BUY FIDELITY LIFE ASSURANCE CO. FOR NZ$118 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial services company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tower Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that it has filed a takeover notice to buy 100% of unlisted Fidelity Life Assurance Co. for NZ$118 million. (published 0033 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 DAEWOO INTERNATIONAL\f28 \uc2 \f2  NEW CHIEF FLAGS CLOSER TIES WITH POSCO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daewoo International Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s new chief executive Friday outlined plans to deepen ties between the South Korean trading and resources firm and its new owner Posco, saying the two companies could advance into overseas markets, especially emerging ones, through projects that will combine the development of energy resources with infrastructure construction. (published 0356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FONTERRA: FARMERS HAVE APPLIED FOR NZ$61 MILLION WORTH OF SHARES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Farmer-shareholders of Fonterra Dairy Co-operative Group Ltd. have applied to buy NZ$61 million of additional Fonterra shares, lifting the number of so-called "dry" shares to 6% of total shares on issue, the dairy giant said Friday. (published 0238 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BILLABONG STRIKES DEAL ON SURF DIVE'N'SKI, JETTY SURF RETAIL BANNERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Surfwear retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Billabong International Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it has struck a deal to buy the Surf Dive 'n' Ski and Jetty Surf retail banners, along with two licensed Billabong stores, from the General Pants Group as it looks to boost its footprint in Australasia. (published 2310 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =KINGFISHER CEO: NEEDS ANOTHER YEAR TO ASSESS CHINA TURNAROUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kingfisher PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  needs another year to "have a sense of where we stand" in its beleaguered China business, Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ian Cheshire\f28 \uc2 \f2  said, though the unit is on track to break even or turn a small profit in 2011. (published 2256 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PUBLICIS\f28 \uc2 \f2 : TO BUY MAJORITY STAKE IN TWO INDIAN MEDIA FIRMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French advertising giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Publicis Groupe SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  Friday said it has signed an agreement to acquire a majority stake in India's public relations and technology communications firm 20:20 MEDIA and social media consulting firm 2020Social, without disclosing the price. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA GOVERNMENT SIGNS DIGITAL ECONOMY MEMORANDUM WITH INTEL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian Government has signed a memorandum of understanding with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intel Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  as it pushes ahead with plans to build a A$43 billion national broadband network, Communications Minister Stephen Conroy said Friday. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CITY DEVELOPMENTS: TO SELL SINGAPORE PROPERTY TO OXLEY CONSORTIUM FOR S$215M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 City Developments Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it plans to sell its 138 Robinson Road office property in Singapore to Oxley Consortium Pte. Ltd for S$215 million. (published 0458 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE EXCHANGE CEO: TO SEEK STAKEHOLDERS' VIEWS ON CONTINUOUS TRADING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore Exchange Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Magnus Bocker\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday the bourse will launch a consultation paper in a few weeks on continuous trading on the exchange. (published 0219 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JUBILANT ORGANOSYS\f28 \uc2 \f2  OFFERS TO BUY OUT CADISTA FOR $0.30/SHARE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jubilant Organosys Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday said a unit of it has commenced a tender offer to buy the shares it currently doesn't own in Cadista Holdings Inc. for $0.30 apiece. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SEMBAWANG ENGINEERS: WON S$180.6 MLN CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 01-10-10 0710GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sembawang Engineers and Constructors, a unit of India's Punj Lloyd Group, said Friday it has won a S$180.6 million tender from the Singapore government's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Public Utilities Board\f28 \uc2 \f2  to construct a waterworks facility. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SIAM CEMENT SELLS 75% STAKE IN INDUSTRIAL ESTATE FIRM FOR THB760 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Siam Cement PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday that it has sold its remaining 75% stake in SIL Industrial Land Co. to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hemaraj Land & Development PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a deal worth THB760 million . (published 0203 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IP E-GAME PLANS TO RAISE PHP134.2 MLN STOCK RIGHTS OFFER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IP E-Game Ventures Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a Philippine online games provider, Friday said its board approved a stock rights offering that will give its shareholders the right to buy four new shares for every one share held. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MARUTI SUZUKI, TVS MOTOR POST HIGHEST-EVER MONTHLY SALES IN SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Maruti Suzuki India Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 TVS Motor Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . both posted their highest-ever monthly sales in September as dealers bought more motorcycles and cars in anticipation of a sharp rise in demand during the two-month festive season that starts this month. (published 0537 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY UP; BARGAIN HUNTING AIDS TOKYO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly higher Friday, with some beaten down stocks in Tokyo attracting buyers amid hopes the Bank of Japan will announce additional monetary easing measures to support the economy at its policy meet next week. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: INPEX MULLING EXIT FROM IRAN AZADEGAN OIL FIELD -METI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Minister of Economy, Trade and Industry Akihiro Ohata said Friday that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Inpex Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is considering an exit from Iran's Azadegan oil field. (published 0429 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: INDIA LIFTS BAN ON SUGAR FUTURES AS OUTPUT SET TO RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India has lifted a ban on sugar futures trade it had imposed in May 2009, as production of the sweetener is likely to improve substantially in the marketing year that started Friday, the head of the commodity futures market regulator said. (published 0614 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INDIA CANCELS TENDERS FOR GRAIN DELIVERIES TO BANGLADESH -TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India has cancelled tenders seeking bids from private companies to transport 500,000 metric tons of wheat and rice from government stockpiles to Bangladesh, trading executives familiar with the developments said Friday. (published 0540 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN METI MINISTER: TO MAINTAIN TARGET OF 25% CUT IN EMISSIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan will maintain a target to cut carbon dioxide emissions by 25% from 1990 levels by 2020, as long as all major emitter countries are committed to an international framework, Japan's new Minister of Economy, Trade and Industry, Akihiro Ohata, said Friday. (published 0524 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: FAO FOOD PRICE INDEX HITS 25-MONTH HIGH ON CEREALS, SUGAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Food and Agriculture Organization Friday revised its monthly Food Price Index to a 25-month high, mainly due to higher global cereal and sugar prices, though the United Nations agency said the measure probably won't test an historic high reached in mid-2008. (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SK ENERGY BOARD APPROVES PLAN TO SPIN OFF REFINING, CHEMICAL BUSINESSES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SK Energy Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., South Korea's largest oil refiner by capacity, said Friday that its board has approved a restructuring plan, under which it will spin off its refining and chemical businesses into two separate companies. (published 0149 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =OIL DATA: S KOREA SEPTEMBER CRUDE IMPORTS VALUE UP 16.1% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar value of South Korea's crude-oil imports rose 16.1% from a year earlier to $5.64 billion in September, as Korean manufacturers ramped up exports, reflecting still-robust demand for their products despite widespread concerns about the strength of the global economic recovery. (published 0128 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BPMIGAS: GAS PIPELINE LEAK MAY CUT OIL OUTPUT IN RIAU BY 150,000 B/D \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A natural gas pipeline leakage in Sumatra could cut crude-oil production in Riau by as much as 150,000 barrels a day, dealing a blow to the government's effort to meet a production target. (published 0113 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA OFFICIAL: 2,000 MW HYDROELECTRIC CAPACITY EXPANSION FACES DELAYS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's plans to add 2,000 megawatts of hydroelectric capacity from 2012 to 2017 could be delayed by environmental issues, a power ministry official said Friday. (published 0618 GMT) [ 01-10-10 0710GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101001e6a1000ge\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
