Cheung Kong (0001.HK), \uc2 SHK Properties\uc2  (0016.HK). Overall, given HSI's about 9% gain in September, "we believe the market will enter a period of consolidation over the next few trading sessions," says \uc2 Celestial Securities\uc2 . (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0429 GMT [Dow Jones] PREVIEW: Hong Kong August retail sales growth likely remained in double digits, but likely slowed vs July on fading base factor. By value, tipped +16.0% on-year in August vs July's +18.9%; by volume +13.2% in August vs July's +16.0%, according to Dow Jones poll of 5 economists. "Domestic demand remains buoyant with the fall in the jobless rate and tourist arrivals continue to be resilient, but the higher base of comparison last year also weighs on the headline figure," Core Pacific-Yamaichi analyst Keith Lo says. \uc2 Bank of East Asia\uc2  economist Paul Tang says retail sales growth likely fell to "high single digits" in 4Q due to higher base of comparison, as city's retail sales returned to growth since September last year. Data due 0830 GMT Monday. (chester.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0424 GMT [Dow Jones] While central banks of South Korea, Singapore, Thailand and Indonesia were suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets overnight, following confirmed moves by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month, don't expect \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  to do any such thing, say traders and strategists. With surging mining sector, robust banking system, inflation a very real concern, RBA is looking to cool the economy any way it can, with gains in AUD helping \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "If the Aussie dollar wasn't as high as it is, we could see more than one rate hike by the end of the year as it's doing some heavy lifting for the RBA. A high Aussie dollar curbs importers and inflation, creating a dampening affect that is exactly what the RBA wants," says \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  Economist Helen Kevans. AUD/USD last at 0.9670 after hitting 26-month high around 0.9730 overnight. (geoffrey.rogow@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0423 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares end +0.3% at 454.52, with buying led by foreigners on 3Q earnings hopes, also ahead of key government meeting later this week, though concerns on high interest rates remain. "Institutions continue to buy with faith that the government will have to work out new measures to support the economy in 4Q, amid rising worries that high interest rates will hurt company profitability and also discourage borrowing," says Hanoi-based fund management analyst. Volume average at 40.6 million shares valued at VND1.21 trillion. Among most active, Ocean Group (OGC.VH) ends down 1.9% at VND31,600, \uc2 Thuan Thao Corp\uc2 . (GTT.VH) ends +4.5% at VND11,500, \uc2 Sacombank\uc2  (STB.VH) ends +1.2% at VND16,700. Tips stronger sentiment tomorrow; key index to move in 455-460 range. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0418 GMT [Dow Jones] Nomura Securities says BOJ September quarterly tankan result, in which large manufacturers' diffusion index (DI) difference (between current survey and previous survey forecast) declined from +9 in June to +5, is consistent with revision index of analysts' earnings forecasts for manufacturers in Nomura 400 index, which remained positive but contracted between June and September. "Against this backdrop, we think upward revisions to analyst forecasts or company guidance are unlikely to provide support for share prices," writes analyst Ryota Sakagami in report. However, says forecast DIs are below current business conditions DIs for almost all sectors, setting the stage for possible positive surprises ahead. Adds, sectors likely to post positive earnings surprises relative to guidance include electrical machinery, motor vehicles, chemicals, ceramics makers, and pulp and paper makers. (bradford.frischkorn@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0414 GMT [Nikkei/Dow Jones] Office and medical equipment leasing firm Ricoh Leasing (8566.TO) up 2.8% at Y2,088, off high of Y2,120, as company revises up net profit outlook. Shares now up more than 4.0% from 4-week low of Y1,997 on Tuesday when they went ex-dividend for 1H ending September 30. Firm now expects 22% rise in this FY net profit outlook to Y8.1 billion vs previously estimated Y6.9 billion as fall in corporate bankruptcies lead to lower loan provisions, interest rate falls reduce fund-raising costs. Shares now up 13% year-to-date. (kazuhiro.shimamura@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0412 GMT [Dow Jones] NZD/USD weaker after soft building consents data, business confidence survey but still rangebound, held up by weaker USD, says \uc2 Westpac\uc2  Bank Senior Market Strategist Imre Speizer. Pair last 0.7359 vs 0.7385 early in NZ; "The flavor of the day has been more poor data. Confidence is dribbling off, building activity is weaker than most economists expected." But says as long as USD weakness remains dominant theme, "the Kiwi probably won't fall as much as it probably should." Tips Kiwi to remain 0.7320-0.7340 range. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0412 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex off 0.1% at 19,948.16 as traders tread cautiously before September derivatives expiry later today. "Trading is subdued. There is some short-covering in select bluechips, mainly financials after yesterday's decline," says dealer at domestic brokerage. Adds, volume tepid, Sensex expected in 19,900-20,160 range. Says, trading activity could pick up towards the close. HDFC (500010.BY), +1.8% at INR719, top gainer, while \uc2 Reliance Communications (532712.BY) \uc2 off 0.8% at INR168.40. \uc2 Hindustan Unilever\uc2  (500696.BY) +0.8% at INR308.20, ICICI Bank (532174.BY) +0.3% at INR1,104.50. Mahindra (500520.BY) down 0.8% at INR693.15, \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY) down 0.6% at INR993.50. (gurdev.singh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0410 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CNY remains up midday but trims some earlier gains as pair faces downward pressure on pre-holiday bank customers' demand for CNY, despite higher-than-expected USD/CNY fixing; on OTC, USD/CNY at 6.6907 vs 6.6868 last close, after trading in 6.6887-6.6960 morning; "There's heavy dollar selling pressure, but there has been demand around 6.6900," says Shanghai-based trader at European bank, adding sustained USD bids both on OTC, anonymous automatic price-matching system around 6.6900 likely PBOC-guided flows. "There's consensus in the market that the yuan will continue to appreciate, likely until November, even though the scale of the appreciation won't be nearly as large as the U.S. is hoping for." USD/CNY tipped 6.6850-6.6950 remainder of session. (joy.shaw@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0406 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 ANZ Bank\uc2  is latest to turn up at AUD/USD parity party, predicting pair to hit 1.0000 some time in 2011, though it will be brief. ANZ's Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategist, Grant Turley, is an ex RBA official and spent time in their New York dealing room so his views will catch attention. Says while parity is likely, there's some risk of a short-term correction and recommends selling before 0.9850, then buy at 0.9300. Says USD will pick up in mid 2011 as U.S. recovers, but AUD still has edge. "This will boost the USD against all \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but our expectations of an aggressive rate hike cycle from the RBA, and further rises in the terms of trade through 2011, will mean that the AUD remains strong into this USD strength." Pair last at 0.9675. (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0404 GMT [Dow Jones] LME 3-month copper at $8,002/ton, down $61 with 2,000 lots done but off early low of $7,953/ton as fears of big sell-off in Shanghai recede. SHFE December copper plunged CNY3,360 or $502 early but move was brief and not reflected in other Shanghai contracts. "It's fair to say the market (LME) was a trifle confused when that Shanghai price came in. It did seem out of whack with what was going on but it sparked some fairly heavy selling," says Hong Kong based LME broker. Adds, Shanghai has recovered but December copper still down CNY560 at CNY60,080 in line with other copper contracts. Outlook for copper later in trading day mixed; notes, though trend recently for London to buy copper back up on weak dollar, he's unsure how long current bull feeling in London will be sustained. Adds, "Shanghai is still trading resolutely below LME levels so the bullish feeling is obviously not shared where it matters." SHFE January contract trading at more than $350 discount at the moment. (james.campbell@dowjones.com) [ 09-30-10 0041ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100930e69u0002z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
