\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Taiwan Central Bk May Pause After Thu-MONEY TALKS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2010\par 07:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0501 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely to hold rates steady until at least end-2010, if it delivers a 12.5bp hike Thursday as widely expected. What likely worries \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  most: rising TWD, hot money flows; it's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily on almost daily basis over past months to cap TWD gains lest it damages export-dependent economy. As Fed may embark on fresh round of quantitative easing by year-end, more easy money will probably come to Asia; Taiwan can't risk drawing more speculative funds that could potentially inflate asset price bubble, with home prices in major city such as Taipei already up 10% over past year. Slowing exports, fragile global economic backdrop also back view \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stand pat. See "=MONEY TALKS: Taiwan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Likely To Pause After Thu." (aries.poon@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0459 GMT [Dow Jones] India overnight call rate rises to over 6-month high due to strong demand from banks to secure cash near quarter's end, says dealer with state-run bank; interbank call rate at RBI's negotiated dealing system at 7.30% vs 7% at Tuesday's close, collateralized borrowing and lending obligation or CBLO firm at 6.66%; both above \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's repo rate of 6.00%. "The system is short of cash as about INR500 billion has flowed as advance tax payment in mid-month which is yet to return back as government spending," says dealer. Tips call rates, CBLO to stay above repo rate of 6.00%. Banks typically hold on to cash at quarter end, aggravating shortage in interbank market. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0458 GMT [Dow Jones] Kospi extends gains, last +0.8% at 1870.64 with foreign investors snapping up technology shares, left out in recent sessions after a run-up. Positive overnight lead from U.S. markets, expectations of further quantitative easing steps by U.S. Fed also boosting sentiment, traders say; "Foreigners are looking for bargains on expectations the market will continue to be driven by ample liquidity," says Mirae Asset Securities analyst Lee Jin-woo. Tips 1900 resistance for now. LG Display (034220.SE) +4.8% at KRW39,400, Hynix (000660.SE) +3.5% at KRW22,100. \uc2 Korea Exchange Bank\uc2  (004940.SE) off 2.5% at KRW13,600 on profit-taking. Foreign investors net buyers of shares worth KRW249 billion. (in-soo.nam@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0452 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/KRW briefly falls below key 1,140 mark for first time since May 14; but recovers from 1,139.8 intraday low to trade at 1,140.1 amid "extremely high concern that the BOK could step in to smooth the won's rise," says foreign bank trader. Pair has been hovering around 1,140 since late morning amid tug of war between export settlement, short-covering, but breaking, settling at lower levels "a matter of time" amid broad weakness of USD. Traders say some importers also seen in market. (kanga.kong@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0445 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CNY still down midday following record low USD/CNY central parity rate (6.6936 vs 6.7051 yesterday), strong EUR gains vs USD overnight; on OTC, USD/CNY at 6.6857, after touching 6.6844, lowest intraday level under current system, vs 6.6906 last close; tipped 6.6800-6.6950 for rest of session. "the yuan's strength is in line with non-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' gains," says Shanghai-based trader at Japanese bank. "If the euro rises above $1.3600 later today, it's possible for the dollar to fall below 6.6800." But adds, USD selling pressure not as heavy as past two days, as pre-holiday, quarter-end \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlement rush mostly took place in last 2 days. Transactions today, tomorrow to settle after long holiday (China markets to close Oct. 1-Oct. 7 for National Day holiday). (joy.shaw@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0443 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares end down 0.5% at 452.94 as local retailers sell on concerns over high interest rates. "Some players are also selling stocks to buy dollars due to Vietnam's rising trade deficit," says trader. Adds, players likely to stay on sidelines ahead of key government meeting later this week; investors waiting for government to step in with new financial measures to help boost economy in 4Q. Volume thin with 33.2 million shares valued at VND897 trillion. Among most active, Ocean Group (OGC.VH) ends flat at VND32,200, Saigon Securities (SSI.VH) ends down 1.5% at VND27,000, \uc2 Sacombank\uc2  (STB.VH) ends down 3.0% at VND16,500. Tips support for key index at 445. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0441 GMT [Dow Jones] If HSI ends today in positive territory, index will have risen 17 of 20 trading sessions so far in September, notes futures trader. "Market's strength is unmistakable," he says; although market clearly overbought, says traders better not go short as market can go from strength to strength. HSI +1.3% at 22,392.09 midday, taking cue from Wall Street; volume solid at HK$46.10 billion, in part boosted by combined HK$3.16 billion from today's 2 debutantes; HSI's year-to-date high of 22,671 eyed next. Chalco (2600.HK) leads blue-chips' rally, +5.2% at HK$7.70 on top of 4.3% gain yesterday, which came on parent's CNY10 billion plan to invest in rare earth resources. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0438 GMT [Dow Jones] KLCI +0.2% at 1462.46, trapped in narrow 6-point range throughout morning session in subdued trading; some 426 million shares traded by midday, among lowest levels in recent days. Range-bound trading pattern likely to persist rest of day as participants mostly content to stay on sidelines in absence of fresh leads, dealers say. RHB Research says while KLCI's longer-term uptrend intact, with support at 1450, index must break 1467 (10-day moving average) to regain bullish momentum in the near-term; says in meantime, "local market sentiment will continue to be influenced by volatility in the overseas markets." Among gainers, Gamuda (5398.KU) +1.6% at MYR3.86 after reporting 77% jump in 4Q FY10 earnings, UEM Land (5148.KU) +5.4% at MYR2.13 on upbeat outlook for property demand. Among decliners, AirAsia (5099.KU) down 2.8% at MYR2.08 on profit-taking after recent rally to record high. (benjamin.low@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0437 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore shares holding above water but further gains limited as investors cautious after solid gains recently. STI +0.5% at 3112.62 midday, with immediate resistance at year-to-date high of 3125. Market breadth at over 3 gainers for every decliner, but overall volume light at 1.06 billion shares worth S$931.9 million, with Genting Singapore (G13.SG), \uc2 Genting Hong Kong\uc2  (S21.SG) most active. Genting Singapore +0.5% at S$1.96, \uc2 Genting Hong Kong\uc2  +4.7% at US$0.45, recouping part of yesterday's hefty losses prompted by Genting Singapore CEO's stake reduction via sale in open market. "The market is not doing that badly. Some profit-taking is to be expected as prices cannot go up everyday," says broker at Singapore bank. (frankie.ho@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0437 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei up 0.8% at 9568.20, helped by gains in Asian markets, strong China PMI data, say market analysts. "Strong Chinese markets are suggesting that economic sentiment is good," says Kazuhiro Takahashi, general manager at Daiwa Securities Capital Markets. Also says as for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, there are hopes for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (as USD/JPY trading below 84) and additional monetary easing measures from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , therefore investors may stay on sidelines or now. Index resistance seen at 9600. Exporters generally higher on strong tankan data; \uc2 Nissan Motor\uc2  (7201.TO) up 3.0% at Y747, \uc2 Sony\uc2  (6758.TO) up 2.1% at Y2,648, \uc2 Nippon Yusen\uc2  (9101.TO) up 2.9% at Y349. \uc2 Tokyo Electric Power\uc2  (9501.TO) off 7.7% at Y2,106 on over 6X normal full-day volume on capital increase reports, dragging entire Topix electric power & gas sector down 2.8%. (ayai.tomisawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0435 GMT [Dow Jones] JGBs up on view that additional BOJ policy-easing now "just a matter of time," as tankan survey suggests economy will likely fall into a lull with business sentiment index for large manufacturers expected to fall to minus 1 in December survey, 1st deterioration in 7 quarters, Mitsubishi UFJ Morgan Stanley Securities senior strategist Naomi Hasegawa says. "There are just so may bad factors for the economy going into the second half of fiscal 2010," she says, such as end to government incentive program to buy fuel-efficient cars, strong JPY. Lead December futures last 143.25, up 0.20 while 10-year yield last down 2.5 bps at 0.935%.(takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0433 GMT [Dow Jones] Philippine shares end lower, reversing early-session gains, as investors take profit following recent gains. Bellwether PSEi off 0.3% to 4111.05 in heavy volume vs 4142 intraday high. "The market has been up a lot so there's need for a healthy profit-taking," says Jose Vistan, AB Capital Securities research head. Expects benchmark index to test 4000 support in near term; next resistance at 4130. Among most actives, Metro Pacific Investments (MPI.PH) unchanged at PHP3.80; Energy Development (EDC.PH) off 3.5% at PHP6.25, Metropolitan Bank (MBT.PH) off 1.7% at PHP70.60. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com) [ 09-29-10 0101ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100929e69t0003h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
